            <a href="/vin-decoder/" id="vinCheckerBtn" class="px-8 py-4 rounded-xl btn-primary text-white font-bold text-base whitespace-nowrap tracking-wide text-center">
              Check VIN
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">What Does a VIN Checker Do?</h2>
        <p class="text-silver-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">A VIN checker takes a vehicle's unique 17-character identification number and decodes it into readable information. Each position in the VIN encodes specific data about the vehicle — from the country of manufacture to the assembly plant and production sequence.</p>
        <p class="text-silver-400 leading-relaxed mb-6">When you run a VIN check through Car Alpha, you get the complete vehicle profile: make, model, year, engine specifications, body type, trim level, drive type, and — critically — any open NHTSA safety recalls that may affect the vehicle.</p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">When Should You Check a VIN?</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-silver-400 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-volt-400 mt-1">&#x2713;</span> Before buying a used car — verify specs match the listing</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-volt-400 mt-1">&#x2713;</span> After a recall notice — confirm if your vehicle is affected</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-volt-400 mt-1">&#x2713;</span> When selling — provide buyers with verified specifications</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-volt-400 mt-1">&#x2713;</span> For insurance quotes — ensure accurate vehicle details</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-volt-400 mt-1">&#x2713;</span> During maintenance — order correct parts for your exact build</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

